	<title>Troubleshooting — Pontia</title>
	<meta name="description" content="Diagnose Pontia service, Dashboard, Agent Client, and remote-access problems." />
</svelte:head>

# Troubleshooting

Start with Pontia's diagnostic report:

```sh
pontia doctor
```

Each line explains a service, configuration, login, or remote-registration check and suggests a repair when needed. If configuration changed, restart the service with `pontia up`.

## The service does not start

Validate `$PONTIA_HOME/config.toml` for invalid TOML, unknown values, inaccessible paths, or a port already in use. The default address is `127.0.0.1:8080`.

On Linux, inspect the user service:

```sh
systemctl --user status pontia.service --no-pager --full
journalctl --user -u pontia.service --no-pager -n 200
```

On macOS, inspect the LaunchAgent:

```sh
launchctl print gui/$(id -u)/dev.pontia.pontiad
```

`pontia up` refreshes the service definition using the current Pontia executable and restarts an existing service. `pontia down` stops and disables the Pontia service. Agent Clients manage their native conversations separately.

## The local Dashboard does not open

1. Run `pontia status` and resolve service errors first.
2. Use <http://127.0.0.1:8080/dashboard> unless `bind_addr` uses another port.
3. Enter the `external_api_token` from `$PONTIA_HOME/config.toml`.
4. If a custom Dashboard archive is configured, verify `[dashboard].source`. Remove that override to return to the release-matched Dashboard.

Keep the External API token private. See [Security](/docs/security) for guidance on sharing diagnostics.

## No Workspace is available

Check the configured roots in [Workspaces](https://app.pontia.dev/workspaces). A directory can be activated only when it exists and is inside an available root. If a root moved, update `[workspace_browser].roots` in `config.toml`, restart Pontia, then revoke stale Workspace registrations from the Dashboard.

## pi cannot start or report activity

Verify:

```sh
pi --version
tmux -V
```

Run `pontia setup pi` to reinstall the plugin. Inspect:

```text
$PONTIA_HOME/state/pi-hook.log
```

Also check a custom `[runtime.pi].tui_command` for an invalid path or wrapper.

## Codex cannot connect

Confirm that your Codex build supports the app-server daemon, then inspect its per-user service. See [Codex](/docs/codex) for platform commands. Run `pontia setup codex` if the executable or `CODEX_HOME` changed, or if the launcher or its shell PATH configuration is missing.

Command, file-change, and permission approvals appear in the Dashboard. An agent can still appear stuck when Codex waits for another kind of request that the Dashboard does not show. Interrupt the Turn if needed, then adjust the Codex policy or answer the request in the native Codex interface.

## Claude Agent cannot start

Check that `node --version` and `npm --version` work for the user that runs Pontia, then run `pontia setup claude-agent` to re-run the dependency check. If the Dashboard reports an authentication failure while the SDK retries, fix Claude Code's own login or provider settings for that user. See the [Claude Agent guide](https://github.com/anthod0/pontia/blob/main/docs/claude-agent.md) to update the client package.

## An ACP agent cannot start

Confirm that the entry's `command` runs for the Pontia service user, and inspect its `effective_config` with `pontia client show AGENT_ID`. The agent must support loading and closing sessions; otherwise the Session reports the missing capability.

## A remote device is offline

On the device:

```sh
pontia status
pontia doctor
```

Check `$PONTIA_HOME/auth.json`, `e2e-identity.json`, and the `[remote]` device ID in `config.toml`. Use `pontia login` and `pontia remote enable` to repair registration, or `pontia remote rotate-key` to replace the device encryption identity.

Verify that the selected Edge is healthy in [Edge settings](/settings/edges). For a self-hosted Edge, check:

```sh
sudo systemctl status pontia-edge.service --no-pager --full
sudo journalctl -u pontia-edge.service --no-pager -n 200
```

## Edge initialization is incomplete

Fix the network, DNS, port, or certificate error reported by the original command, then resume on the same server:

```sh
sudo pontia-edge retry
```

`retry` uses the initialization state saved on the server to continue the existing deployment.

## An update fails

`pontia update` verifies signed release metadata and artifacts before replacing binaries. If service restart or health verification fails, it restores the previous binaries and attempts to recover the service. Inspect the platform service logs, resolve the startup problem, and run the update again.

For further diagnosis, share the output of `pontia --version`, `pontia status`, the operating system, and relevant service errors after removing the sensitive values listed in [Security](/docs/security).
